Applies to stroke-web: the Stroke website, the licence service, the payment
integration, and the free AI proxy.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Plain-English summary (not legally binding — the terms below govern):

  - You CAN read, audit, modify and build this source, and run it yourself for
    development, testing, or to satisfy yourself about what the service does
    with your data.
  - You CANNOT sell it, rebrand it, or run it as a service for other people.
  - You CANNOT use it to issue Stroke licences, or to stand up an alternative
    activation, update, or distribution endpoint for Stroke.
  - The official service runs at stroke.click.

This is the same licence as the Stroke desktop application, deliberately. This
repository is the service that issues and validates the licences that fund
Stroke, and takes payment. A backend on freer terms than the product it licenses
would be an open invitation to strip the gating and reroute the clients.

